        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Edwin Forrest, William Charles Macready, Catherine Norton Sinclair\n- Events: Astor Place Riot\n- Places: Astor Opera House, Manhattan, New York City\n\nFacts:\n- On May 10, 1849, the Astor Place Riot occurred at the now-demolished Astor Opera House in Manhattan, New York City.\n- The Astor Place Riot left at least 25 people dead and more than 120 people injured.\n- Edwin Forrest's feud with the British actor William Charles Macready caused the deadly Astor Place Riot of 1849.\n- Catherine Norton Sinclair's sensational divorce from Edwin Forrest captivated the American public in the mid-1800s.",
